## 2026-05-19 13:17:51 +03 - BE-0570
- What was implemented: Added a provider-neutral billing export abstraction for usage-counter invoicing. Migration `0066_billing_exports` creates tenant-scoped `billing_exports` and immutable `billing_export_items`; `store.BillingExportRepository` prepares idempotent export groups by organization/subscription/period/provider, snapshots `usage_counters`, records provider response ids, and marks failed attempts with redacted summaries plus retry timing. Added `internal/controlplane/billing` with `Provider`, `ProviderFunc`, `ExportBatch`, and `BatchFromStoreExport` so Stripe/manual adapters consume stable snapshots without coupling core metering to provider SDKs.
- Files changed: `internal/controlplane/store/migrate/migrations/0066_billing_exports.up.sql`, `internal/controlplane/store/migrate/migrations/0066_billing_exports.down.sql`, `internal/controlplane/store/billing_export.go`, `internal/controlplane/store/billing_export_repository_test.go`, `internal/controlplane/billing/export.go`, `internal/controlplane/billing/export_test.go`, `internal/controlplane/billing/AGENTS.md`, `ralph/prd.json`, `ralph/progress.txt`.
- Verification run: `gofmt -w .`; `goimports -w .` not run because `goimports` is not installed; `go mod tidy`; `go test ./...`; `go test -race ./...`; `go vet ./...`; `go test ./internal/controlplane/...`; `go test -race ./internal/controlplane/...`; `go test -run TestMigrations ./...`; `go test -run TestPolicyMatrix ./...`; `go test -run TestQuotaConcurrency ./...`; `go test -run TestFakeDokploy ./...`; `golangci-lint run ./...`.
- Results: All executed checks passed. Optional `staticcheck` and `govulncheck` were not run because they are not installed in this environment.
- Remaining risks or follow-ups: Provider-specific adapters and worker scheduling are still future stories; this story establishes the durable snapshot and provider boundary they should use. No public HTTP surface was added, so JSON envelope and auth contract criteria are not applicable in this iteration.
- **Learnings for future iterations:**
  - Billing exports should consume `usage_counters` snapshots, not raw usage events or provider-specific invoices, so retries submit a stable item basis even if later counter replays occur.
  - Keep provider error summaries behind both `output.Redactor` and a provider-token regex before persistence/logging; provider SDK errors can echo auth context.
  - `billing_exports` is tenant-scoped by organization and subscription through a composite FK; cross-tenant subscription/export combinations are unrepresentable at the database layer.
